253
00:12:44,940 --> 00:12:46,260
I'm ordering pizza.

254
00:12:46,580 --> 00:12:49,380
Hey, now look, I spent the last two hours boiling this garbage.

255
00:12:49,460 --> 00:12:51,720
Now nobody leaves until every last liver burger is gone.

256
00:12:53,560 --> 00:12:56,100
Okay. Hey, hey.

257
00:12:56,880 --> 00:12:59,720
Hey, we wanted extra cheese and pepperoni on that pizza.

258
00:12:59,940 --> 00:13:00,780
All right, all right, pal.

259
00:13:00,780 --> 00:13:02,040
You have gone too far this time.

260
00:13:02,240 --> 00:13:04,440
No more telephone for you until Mom and Dad get home.

261
00:13:04,940 --> 00:13:06,100
I don't have to put up with this.

262
00:13:06,220 --> 00:13:07,080
I'm taller than you.

263
00:13:07,880 --> 00:13:09,140
Mike, he's testing you.

264
00:13:09,140 --> 00:13:10,220
You have to draw the line.

265
00:13:10,220 --> 00:13:12,560
Or grow! Ah!

266
00:13:13,920 --> 00:13:16,080
Hey, listen! Come on!

267
00:13:16,360 --> 00:13:20,440
Whoa! Don't worry, you'll be fine!

268
00:13:20,920 --> 00:13:22,700
Ah! Ah! Ah!

269
00:13:23,420 --> 00:13:24,440
Watch your elbows!

270
00:13:24,940 --> 00:13:26,340
It's hurting you!

271
00:13:26,480 --> 00:13:27,600
It's hurting you?

272
00:13:27,920 --> 00:13:29,220
Hey, you sound just like Mom!

273
00:13:29,260 --> 00:13:30,600
Oh, yeah? Does Mom do this?

274
00:13:31,300 --> 00:13:34,140
Ah! Yeah, how do you like that, huh?

275
00:13:34,140 --> 00:13:35,500
You can't hold me down on light bulbs!

276
00:13:35,640 --> 00:13:36,460
You're right, I can't!

277
00:13:36,520 --> 00:13:37,640
Carol, bring me a rope.

278
00:13:49,420 --> 00:13:50,960
Honey, dinner's ready.

279
00:13:54,400 --> 00:13:56,820
Come on, sit over here and take a load off.

280
00:13:58,680 --> 00:14:00,700
I'm sorry I got upset.

281
00:14:01,020 --> 00:14:03,380
That's me who should apologize, not you.

282
00:14:03,960 --> 00:14:06,160
What for? For not bringing your underwear.

283
00:14:06,680 --> 00:14:08,320
This wasn't like the other times.

284
00:14:08,460 --> 00:14:09,600
This was an honest mistake.

285
00:14:10,280 --> 00:14:12,040
Well, that's very sweet, but don't worry.

286
00:14:12,040 --> 00:14:13,120
I'm wearing yours.

287
00:14:14,580 --> 00:14:15,460
What's for dinner?

288
00:14:16,300 --> 00:14:18,320
Marshmallows. That's it?

289
00:14:18,340 --> 00:14:20,400
I'm sorry. I was a little distracted today.

290
00:14:20,400 --> 00:14:21,440
I didn't get to the market.

291
00:14:21,800 --> 00:14:25,040
Oh. I've ruined our whole vacation, haven't I?

292
00:14:25,300 --> 00:14:27,380
Nah. I got lots of marshmallows.

293
00:14:29,500 --> 00:14:32,360
Remember what a terrible time we had the last time we went camping?

294
00:14:32,360 --> 00:14:33,580
You had a great time.

295
00:14:34,120 --> 00:14:34,760
No, no, no.

296
00:14:34,760 --> 00:14:39,120
I'm talking about when Ben and Mike and Carol were babies and Mike had diarrhea and

297
00:14:39,120 --> 00:14:40,760
it rained and everything got all wet.

298
00:14:40,780 --> 00:14:42,180
I'm talking about the same trip.

299
00:14:42,980 --> 00:14:44,480
Well, what was so nice about that?

300
00:14:45,100 --> 00:14:46,640
We were together, Maggie.

301
00:14:48,140 --> 00:14:54,080
And it was so sweet watching you with Mike rocking him in your arms till he fell

302
00:14:54,080 --> 00:14:55,440
asleep, which he never did.

303
00:14:56,800 --> 00:14:58,720
I'd forgotten all about that.

304
00:15:00,060 --> 00:15:01,180
Wasn't that just last week?

305
00:15:01,360 --> 00:15:03,260
No, that was me you rocked last week.

306
00:15:05,280 --> 00:15:08,060
I'd be lucky to get a minute with him nowadays.

307
00:15:08,780 --> 00:15:10,920
Ooh, they grow up in a hurry, don't they?

308
00:15:12,780 --> 00:15:15,160
You know who we sound like?

309
00:15:15,560 --> 00:15:17,400
We sound like our parents talking.

310
00:15:18,460 --> 00:15:22,080
Well, the one joy that I get in all this is that someday

311
00:15:22,860 --> 00:15:27,420
Mike and Carol and Ben and Chrissy are all gonna be sitting around a campfire like

312
00:15:27,420 --> 00:15:32,320
this suddenly dumbstruck at the very thought that they are sounding like old

313
00:15:32,320 --> 00:15:37,220
irrelevant us. You OK?

314
00:15:38,760 --> 00:15:42,360
I want to tell you what I meant today when I said that I wasn't feeling the right

315
00:15:42,360 --> 00:15:51,520
feelings. OK. You know the day of his funeral?

316
00:15:53,180 --> 00:15:55,180
When I saw daddy there in that coffin?

317
00:15:57,120 --> 00:16:00,620
I thought, I thought, what a shame.

318
00:16:00,720 --> 00:16:01,960
Of course, sweetheart.

319
00:16:01,960 --> 00:16:02,800
He's your father.

320
00:16:02,820 --> 00:16:03,780
No, that's not what I mean.

321
00:16:03,780 --> 00:16:05,520
I thought. What?

322
00:16:07,640 --> 00:16:12,080
Well, I thought about all the work and the care he put into raising me.

323
00:16:12,080 --> 00:16:12,820
And in the end, I.

324
00:16:13,920 --> 00:16:17,100
What, honey? It's a horrible thought.

325
00:16:17,700 --> 00:16:18,500
What'd you say?

326
00:16:25,320 --> 00:16:27,260
I didn't need him anymore.

327
00:16:29,440 --> 00:16:31,000
I mean, sure, I loved him.

328
00:16:31,000 --> 00:16:32,780
And I miss him terribly.

329
00:16:32,780 --> 00:16:35,480
But honestly, how much a part of my life was he?

330
00:16:37,080 --> 00:16:41,880
I mean, I never listened to his advice.

331
00:16:41,960 --> 00:16:43,640
His opinions were always nutty.

332
00:16:43,780 --> 00:16:48,080
And sometimes it was just easier to ignore him.

333
00:16:49,620 --> 00:16:51,660
I mean, God help me.

334
00:16:52,300 --> 00:16:55,100
I loved it when he sat at the kids' table at Thanksgiving.

335
00:16:57,420 --> 00:16:59,300
Honey, that's no reason to feel guilty.

336
00:16:59,360 --> 00:17:00,980
That's just the way things work.

337
00:17:00,980 --> 00:17:04,340
Like we were saying about Mike when he was a little baby.

338
00:17:05,060 --> 00:17:08,140
I needed every word you had to say.

339
00:17:08,800 --> 00:17:12,040
And now we've created someone who doesn't listen to anything we have to say.

340
00:17:12,360 --> 00:17:14,120
We've done our job well.

341
00:17:14,180 --> 00:17:15,700
Oh, Jason, don't you see?

342
00:17:16,860 --> 00:17:18,640
One day it's gonna be our turn.

343
00:17:19,160 --> 00:17:23,500
I mean, some day we'll die and one of our kids will be sitting here telling someone

344
00:17:23,500 --> 00:17:26,200
how you and I weren't important to their lives either.

345
00:17:27,800 --> 00:17:32,980
I mean, after all the work we put in, After all the bottles and the dirty diapers

346
00:17:32,980 --> 00:17:36,720
and the birthdays and the vacations, I mean, they won't mean a thing.

347
00:17:38,680 --> 00:17:39,600
What's the point?

348
00:17:40,440 --> 00:17:41,900
Well, that's what's bothering you then.

349
00:17:41,900 --> 00:17:43,000
It's not just your dad.

350
00:17:44,980 --> 00:17:48,380
Well, if that sweet, caring man ended up with someone like me,

351
00:17:49,280 --> 00:17:50,620
what do I have to hope for?

352
00:17:50,620 --> 00:17:52,640
Well, aren't you being just a little pessimistic?

353
00:17:55,680 --> 00:17:57,280
Am I? I mean it, Maggie.

354
00:17:57,360 --> 00:18:00,640
Come on. You influence your kids in a thousand ways.

355
00:18:01,100 --> 00:18:08,500
Mike's charm and Carol's brains and Chrissy's cuteness and Ben's height.

356
00:18:11,600 --> 00:18:13,600
This doesn't bother you at all, does it?

357
00:18:13,600 --> 00:18:17,860
No. No. Jason, that really ticks me off.

358
00:18:21,600 --> 00:18:24,760
You ever notice the way I toast a marshmallow?

359
00:18:24,760 --> 00:18:27,840
Yeah, and that really ticks me off, too.

360
00:18:27,980 --> 00:18:29,420
I do it perfect, Maggie.

361
00:18:30,160 --> 00:18:34,620
Perfect. All nice and even and brown on all sides.

362
00:18:35,680 --> 00:18:38,100
You know who else toasts his marshmallows that way?

363
00:18:38,940 --> 00:18:41,020
No. My dad.

364
00:18:42,580 --> 00:18:44,800
I noticed that just a couple years ago.

365
00:18:45,380 --> 00:18:50,000
And that one small connection, Maggie, made me see that my dad influenced me in

366
00:18:50,000 --> 00:18:52,940
countless ways. Ways I can't even imagine.

367
00:18:53,540 --> 00:18:58,220
Just like your dad has influenced you and just like we will influence our kids.

368
00:18:59,640 --> 00:19:02,960
You know what my dad would say if he heard you talking like this?

369
00:19:03,500 --> 00:19:07,360
No. But I'm sure you do.

370
00:19:10,400 --> 00:19:11,840
I wish I could be sure.

371
00:19:25,420 --> 00:19:29,400
Freeze, Ben! You slept down here?

372
00:19:29,820 --> 00:19:30,960
Sleep? Who slept?

373
00:19:31,260 --> 00:19:33,720
I've been standing guard so the little weasel wouldn't sneak out.

374
00:19:34,600 --> 00:19:36,220
Where's Chrissy? Safe.

375
00:19:36,380 --> 00:19:37,180
She's locked in her room.

376
00:19:37,540 --> 00:19:38,720
Good. You locked her up too?

377
00:19:39,480 --> 00:19:41,180
No, she locked herself in.

378
00:19:41,560 --> 00:19:45,160
Oh. Well, I'm just sorry I gotta let Benny out for school.

379
00:19:45,660 --> 00:19:48,580
Well, I hope you nailed his window shut so he didn't climb down the trellis.

380
00:19:49,600 --> 00:19:57,480
Oh. Let's go.

381
00:19:57,780 --> 00:20:00,080
Meter's running. We didn't call a cab.

382
00:20:01,400 --> 00:20:03,700
Chrissy Siever, drop off at Parkway Preschool.

383
00:20:03,920 --> 00:20:05,380
That's right. Let's go.

384
00:20:06,860 --> 00:20:08,620
You called a cab?

385
00:20:08,780 --> 00:20:10,440
Why in the world did you do that?

386
00:20:10,740 --> 00:20:11,960
I drive you to preschool.

387
00:20:12,220 --> 00:20:15,960
A cab driver is not gonna sing you songs and he's not gonna tell you personal

388
00:20:15,960 --> 00:20:17,620
victory stories. I know.

389
00:20:17,780 --> 00:20:19,060
I checked. Let's go.

390
00:20:20,900 --> 00:20:22,440
Hi, mama. Home.

391
00:20:23,880 --> 00:20:27,940
Uh -huh. Look, I am really sorry, but this has been a mistake.

392
00:20:28,140 --> 00:20:29,560
She's only four years old.

393
00:20:29,740 --> 00:20:30,680
All right, I'm gonna kill him.

394
00:20:31,060 --> 00:20:35,080
You! You kids married too young.

395
00:20:36,720 --> 00:20:38,260
You got another ticket, Mike?

396
00:20:38,540 --> 00:20:42,440
What? Yeah. You're lucky the driver of the car you hit didn't press charges.

397
00:20:44,100 --> 00:20:46,420
And you are gonna pay a lot more than mere money, pal.

398
00:20:46,420 --> 00:20:47,380
Hey, hey, what are you doing?

399
00:20:47,380 --> 00:20:48,880
Ow! Come here, you!

400
00:20:49,160 --> 00:20:49,460
You and Pat!

401
00:20:51,480 --> 00:20:52,520
You and Probe!

402
00:20:53,300 --> 00:20:54,340
Don't touch my eye!

403
00:20:55,660 --> 00:20:58,820
Hey! No, I'm not gonna knock it off!

404
00:20:59,500 --> 00:21:03,240
Hey! Welcome home!

405
00:21:04,780 --> 00:21:05,680
Let him go!

406
00:21:07,420 --> 00:21:10,320
Mommy, am I glad to see you!

407
00:21:11,240 --> 00:21:13,360
Mom, I am so glad you're home early!

408
00:21:14,320 --> 00:21:16,940
Well, if it's paradise, it wasn't all it's cracked up to be.

409
00:21:18,500 --> 00:21:20,320
Anybody want to help me with the bags?

410
00:21:21,000 --> 00:21:25,640
Harold tried to mold me, and Mike tried to give us liver poisoning.

411
00:21:26,640 --> 00:21:30,500
Mom, I don't know how you put up with her, especially after you did such a good job

412
00:21:30,500 --> 00:21:32,060
with me. Rope burns, Mom.

413
00:21:32,100 --> 00:21:33,520
Rope burns. Need I say more?

414
00:21:34,100 --> 00:21:37,140
And then he even told me that this was hurting him more than it was hurting me, and

415
00:21:37,140 --> 00:21:38,380
that someday I'd thank him for it.

416
00:21:38,620 --> 00:21:39,820
That's what I say.

417
00:21:40,080 --> 00:21:41,380
Yeah, he's gone nuts.

418
00:21:42,240 --> 00:21:43,380
Mike, did you say that?

419
00:21:43,700 --> 00:21:45,820
Look, I just opened my mouth and it came out.

420
00:21:46,940 --> 00:21:48,140
It just came out?

421
00:21:48,460 --> 00:21:50,400
Yeah, well, you put it there.

422
00:21:52,580 --> 00:21:58,560
Yeah. More bad news, Mom.

423
00:21:58,740 --> 00:22:00,760
Mike even tried to charge me money to behave.

424
00:22:01,460 --> 00:22:03,080
Yeah, I was shocked too.

425
00:22:03,440 --> 00:22:04,580
I don't care.

426
00:22:05,940 --> 00:22:11,660
And worse than that, Carol's victory stories have made me wanna give up completely.

427
00:22:11,840 --> 00:22:13,800
Oh, that's wonderful.

428
00:22:14,400 --> 00:22:17,040
Mom, I don't know how you put up with any of them.

429
00:22:17,260 --> 00:22:21,360
I mean, one day they're gonna realize how great you are and what festering scum they

430
00:22:21,360 --> 00:22:25,220
are. Oh, Carol, sometimes you say the sweetest things.

431
00:22:26,380 --> 00:22:29,040
Oh. Oh. Oh.

432
00:22:29,840 --> 00:22:30,100
Oh.
